<title>AUSTRALIA: OAKFORD PROPERTY UNITS LIST AT A$1.00.</title>
<headline>OAKFORD PROPERTY UNITS LIST AT A$1.00.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Units in Oakford Property Trust made their debut on the Australian Stock Exchange on Thursday at A$1.00, steady with their issue price.</p>
<p>The issue of 18 million units raised A$18 milion and was not underwritten. The Trust's purpose is to assist unlisted apartment management company Oakford Australia Pty Ltd to establish a national chain by developing and owning quality three to four star serviced apartment properties.</p>
<p>By 2.50 p.m. (0250 GMT), Oakford units were at A$1.00, its day high and off a low of 98 cents. Turnover was 51,000 units.</p>
<p>--Walter Watson, Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1810</p>
</text>
